<div class="chapter_content content" id="7682319_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[HISTORY: Adopted by the Common Council of the City of Albany 3-15-1999 by Ord. No. 60.121.98.<a class="footnoteref" href="#ft7682319-1" id="ref7682319-1">[1]</a> Amendments noted where applicable.]</div><aside class="chapterrefblock"><h2 class="generalReferencesTitle">GENERAL REFERENCES</h2><div class="para">Building construction — See Ch. <a class="xref" guid="7681109" href="7681109#7681109">133</a>.</div><div class="para">Commercial standards — See Ch. <a class="xref" guid="7681582" href="7681582#7681582">151</a>.</div><div class="para">Electricity — See Ch. <a class="xref" guid="7682166" href="7682166#7682166">171</a>.</div><div class="para">Fire prevention — See Ch. <a class="xref" guid="7682498" href="7682498#7682498">197</a>.</div><div class="para">Housing — See Ch. <a class="xref" guid="7682800" href="7682800#7682800">231</a>.</div></aside><div class="footnotes"><div class="footnote" id="ft7682319-1"><a class="footnoterefnum" href="#ref7682319-1">[1]</a><div class="ftpara">Editor's Note: This ordinance repealed former Ch. 175, Elevators, adopted 7-18-1983 by L.L. No. 2-1983 as Ch. IXA of the 1983 Code. Said ordinance also stated that it shall take effect 30 days after it shall become law.</div></div></div></div>


